Teleportation; at least if they disappeared completely and nothing
invisible attacked you the next moment. They reappeared somewhere else,
probably very confused and wondering where *you* went when they were
attacking you just a moment ago.

>         Also, I  have a wand  of digging.  How  do I use it,  and what
> does it do?  I kind of like my charachter and don't want to experiment
> by zapping random monsters.

You don't zap monsters with a wand of digging. You dig with it. Zapping
it at a wall will make a doorway; zapping it at solid rock will make a
tunnel (except in some places where there's extra-special hard rock and
you only dig one square at a time); zapping it down (>) will make a
hole in the floor for you to fall through. It doesn't destroy boulders,
which normal digging implements do.

>         Lastly,  (thanks for being  patient and  sorry for  the newbie
> questions) when  I hit t to  throw something there are  not potions in
> the choice, and  applying potions doesn't work.  

There's only one potion you can apply and IIRC it does appear in your
apply list (or perhaps the DevTeam considered that a bug and fixed it).

> If I  want to throw a
> potion of paralyze monster, how do I  do it?  

Just hit * when asked what to throw and you'll get your full inventory
listed. Then select the appropriate inventory letter. Alternatively,
quiver the potion (Q<inventory letter>) and throw it with f<direction>.

> Or do I drink it and the
> monster gets paralyzed?

No, if you drink it *you* get paralyzed, which is Not A Good Idea.

